1
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:11,120
Brighten up the room and try stepping back,
will you?

2
00:00:20,260 --> 00:00:24,300
Anyone without money,
come on over to my place.

3
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:29,000
I don't have any either, but don't worry.

4
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,060
Look at the blue sky,

5
00:00:34,110 --> 00:00:36,300
white clouds.

6
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:42,720
It'll all work out somehow, sooner or later.

7
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:59,920
Anyone without a job,
come on over to my place.

8
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:04,500
I don't have any either, so don't worry.

9
00:01:55,880 --> 00:01:57,020
I'm not that good with my hands.

10
00:01:57,680 --> 00:01:59,460
Eating my bento while reading manga,

11
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:01,560
how can you drink so much beer?

12
00:02:02,420 --> 00:02:04,960
In this day and age,
everything has to be connected, you know.

13
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:07,860
Even lemons watch TV while
munching on rice crackers,

14
00:02:07,860 --> 00:02:09,520
and let out farts, right?

15
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:14,260
The lemon who talked to
Kankichi was an idiot.

16
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:26,460
To Kyoto with Lemon?

17
00:02:27,180 --> 00:02:27,635
Yeah.

18
00:02:27,685 --> 00:02:33,080
Lemon's going to visit her eldest brother, Yuutsu,
at his restaurant, where he's training as a chef in Kyoto.

19
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:37,040
Everyone at the shop is busy this time,
so nobody's free.

20
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:40,280
So that's how I was the one picked

21
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:43,440
Lemon's sensible,
but she's still a kindergartener.

22
00:02:43,440 --> 00:02:45,440
Will you take me with you?

23
00:02:45,920 --> 00:02:49,120
Sure, I can always take time
off at the police box anyway.

24
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:54,320
Lemon's brother Yuutsu is training at a top-class restaurant,
after all.

25
00:02:54,320 --> 00:02:57,920
If I bring Lemon along,
I'll get to enjoy some delicious food.

26
00:03:06,460 --> 00:03:09,360
We will arrive at Nagoya
Station in five minutes.

27
00:03:13,340 --> 00:03:15,940
Oh no, I dropped my ticket.

28
00:03:15,940 --> 00:03:18,220
Where is it?

29
00:03:19,140 --> 00:03:19,540
Here.

30
00:03:21,180 --> 00:03:22,540
Here it is, here it is.

31
00:03:23,060 --> 00:03:24,080
Where are we going?

32
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:25,980
We're changing trains at Nagoya.

33
00:03:25,980 --> 00:03:27,080
Then it's the next stop.

34
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:32,940
Nagoya, Nagoya.

35
00:03:33,920 --> 00:03:36,140
The train will stop here for three minutes.

36
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:38,140
Please mind your step.

37
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:41,220
Thanks, young lady.

38
00:03:42,020 --> 00:03:44,760
Where's the Meitetsu train platform?

39
00:03:48,220 --> 00:03:49,300
Hang on a sec.

40
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:54,060
Show him the train.

41
00:03:54,060 --> 00:03:54,820
Yes.

42
00:03:56,220 --> 00:03:57,180
Sorry to keep you waiting.

43
00:03:57,640 --> 00:03:59,500
I want to take the Meitetsu line.

44
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:01,240
Got it, this way.

45
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:04,260
Thanks for your trouble.

46
00:04:04,260 --> 00:04:05,180
Take care.

47
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:18,660
Aaaah!

48
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:28,040
Did I fall asleep?

49
00:04:30,100 --> 00:04:31,440
Lemon's not here.

50
00:04:31,440 --> 00:04:32,940
Did she go to the bathroom or something?

51
00:04:33,760 --> 00:04:34,640
A phone call?

52
00:04:37,460 --> 00:04:38,500
Yes, hello?

53
00:04:39,520 --> 00:04:41,300
What? I'm at the station!

54
00:04:41,700 --> 00:04:42,740
She got off?

55
00:04:42,740 --> 00:04:44,840
So you're on the platform at Nagoya Station?

56
00:04:45,380 --> 00:04:46,120
Got it.

57
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:47,940
Don't you dare move from there.

58
00:04:49,180 --> 00:04:49,760
Wait right there.

59
00:04:57,820 --> 00:04:58,200
Alright.

60
00:05:13,740 --> 00:05:14,800
Durian

61
00:05:19,140 --> 00:05:21,660
I feel like someone just walked by.

62
00:05:21,660 --> 00:05:22,320
No way!

63
00:05:26,780 --> 00:05:30,000
An inbound train is now
arriving at Platform 15.

64
00:05:30,820 --> 00:05:34,480
He's coming back from Kyoto,
so it'll be another hour.

65
00:05:39,300 --> 00:05:40,320
Sorry to keep you waiting.

66
00:05:42,160 --> 00:05:42,980
Kankichi.

67
00:05:43,620 --> 00:05:45,800
Sorry for leaving you alone.

68
00:05:46,920 --> 00:05:48,640
Yeah, but you got here fast.

69
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:53,180
I jumped off the bullet train
right after I got your call.

70
00:05:53,180 --> 00:05:56,340
And look, I'm in one piece.

71
00:05:58,020 --> 00:05:59,720
Thanks, Kankichi.

72
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:01,160
Don't mention it.

73
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:04,480
Hold on a second.

74
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:08,000
What's your relationship to that girl?

75
00:06:09,020 --> 00:06:12,340
She looks like a child someone
filed a missing persons report for.

76
00:06:13,060 --> 00:06:14,840
She's my relative's child.

77
00:06:19,260 --> 00:06:20,640
Not similar at all.

78
00:06:21,040 --> 00:06:23,220
And you look extremely suspicious.

79
00:06:23,920 --> 00:06:26,580
Anyway,
let's hear the details at the office.

80
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:29,940
Damn it, I'm a police officer, look!

81
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:32,260
This is a well-made fake.

82
00:06:33,400 --> 00:06:36,220
Don't tell lies that are easily exposed.
Just come with me!

83
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:38,902
So what!

84
00:06:38,952 --> 00:06:42,080
Just contact Chief Ohara at Katsushika
station and you'll know right away!

85
00:06:42,840 --> 00:06:45,680
Yes, oh yes, that's right.
No doubt about it.

86
00:06:46,200 --> 00:06:48,053
She's a child from Ryotsu's relatives.

87
00:06:48,103 --> 00:06:50,800
I'm the one who should
apologize for the trouble.

88
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:54,240
Looks like you were
mistaken for a kidnapper.

89
00:06:54,620 --> 00:06:57,180
Well, if it's Ryo-chan and Lemon-chan,
there's nothing to be done.

90
00:06:57,660 --> 00:06:58,380
Right?

91
00:06:59,100 --> 00:07:00,640
Kyoto, Kyoto.

92
00:07:09,900 --> 00:07:10,700
Not again.

93
00:07:10,700 --> 00:07:13,720
Yes, they called earlier as well,

94
00:07:14,300 --> 00:07:17,400
at this rate, he'll probably
cause some trouble in Kyoto too.

95
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:19,120
He might, you know.

96
00:07:20,260 --> 00:07:22,700
I had no idea he was
really a police officer.

97
00:07:22,700 --> 00:07:24,580
I'm terribly sorry for my rudeness.

98
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:28,020
Forget it, I'm not bothered. See you.

99
00:07:28,020 --> 00:07:28,840
Bye-bye.

100
00:07:30,340 --> 00:07:34,080
First they mistake me in Nagoya too.
I'm really out of luck.

101
00:07:34,080 --> 00:07:38,400
Kankichi gets mistaken for a criminal because
he has a shifty look and suspicious clothes.

102
00:07:38,400 --> 00:07:39,220
Leave me alone!

103
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:48,560
It should be around here.

104
00:07:48,560 --> 00:07:50,600
Kankichi, it's that shop over there.

105
00:07:56,980 --> 00:08:00,360
This place, really? It looks like
a pretty high-class restaurant.

106
00:08:00,360 --> 00:08:03,480
I came here with Grandma last year,
so there's no mistake.

107
00:08:04,080 --> 00:08:05,100
Yes, hello, Kankichi.

108
00:08:05,700 --> 00:08:06,980
Gibo-shi Yū-tsu?

109
00:08:07,640 --> 00:08:08,960
Isn't that Yū-san you mean?

110
00:08:09,240 --> 00:08:10,400
That's right.

111
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:12,180
I'll go and get him right now.

112
00:08:12,180 --> 00:08:13,360
Please wait inside.

113
00:08:20,980 --> 00:08:21,920
Lemon

114
00:08:21,920 --> 00:08:22,700
Yū-san

115
00:08:25,760 --> 00:08:27,280
Thanks for coming.

116
00:08:27,280 --> 00:08:28,380
You've gotten heavier.

117
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:30,600
Really.

118
00:08:34,080 --> 00:08:37,380
Just like... what a handsome man,
enough to make you swoon.

119
00:08:37,380 --> 00:08:41,140
Are you by any chance the
one from Grandma's email?

120
00:08:41,140 --> 00:08:43,060
You're Ryotsu Bakakichi-san, right?

121
00:08:43,840 --> 00:08:45,240
Yeah, it's Kankichi.

122
00:08:45,700 --> 00:08:48,920
I thought that was a pretty
bold name to be his real one.

123
00:08:48,920 --> 00:08:51,000
Damn Gepard!

124
00:08:51,620 --> 00:08:53,640
She really is a cute little sister,
isn't she?

125
00:08:53,640 --> 00:08:55,240
She looks just like Yū-san.

126
00:08:55,240 --> 00:08:57,060
How old are you?

127
00:08:57,060 --> 00:08:58,020
Five years old.

128
00:08:58,020 --> 00:08:59,820
This one's a brother, too.

129
00:08:59,820 --> 00:09:02,340
No, he's a relative from Asakusa.

130
00:09:04,080 --> 00:09:04,580
That's right.

131
00:09:04,580 --> 00:09:06,480
Your faces are totally different.

132
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:07,100
Leave him be.

133
00:09:11,820 --> 00:09:12,620
Cheers!

134
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:19,580
Sake tastes great when
you drink it on a trip.

135
00:09:21,020 --> 00:09:23,040
The sake in Kyoto is really good.

136
00:09:23,040 --> 00:09:24,500
Yeah, it's really delicious.

137
00:09:24,500 --> 00:09:26,220
As expected of Matoi's older brother.

138
00:09:26,220 --> 00:09:28,100
He's manly and dashing, isn't he?

139
00:09:28,920 --> 00:09:29,560
No, not really.

140
00:09:29,560 --> 00:09:32,260
Matoi is actually supposed to be feminine.

141
00:09:34,200 --> 00:09:37,840
He wasn't that manly when he was little.

142
00:09:38,720 --> 00:09:40,960
That's because his mother was a
Japanese classical dance teacher.

143
00:09:40,960 --> 00:09:43,820
Matoi also learned dancing from a young age.

144
00:09:44,460 --> 00:09:48,640
When Matoi was in kindergarten,
she was a cute girl with big eyes.

145
00:09:49,120 --> 00:09:51,260
That's hard to imagine.

146
00:09:51,260 --> 00:09:53,920
Wasn't he playing youth baseball?

147
00:09:54,320 --> 00:09:55,680
That was because of me.

148
00:09:55,680 --> 00:10:00,980
I wanted a little brother,
so I taught Matoi baseball.

149
00:10:00,980 --> 00:10:03,040
So that's why he's so good at baseball.

150
00:10:04,080 --> 00:10:06,520
He has a great knack for it,
so he just kept getting better.

151
00:10:08,180 --> 00:10:10,300
Because of that, Matoi quit Hibu

152
00:10:10,300 --> 00:10:13,140
and ended up devoted only
to baseball and softball.

153
00:10:13,800 --> 00:10:15,700
If only I hadn't taught him baseball...

154
00:10:17,600 --> 00:10:19,380
My sister was supposed to act ladylike.

155
00:10:23,440 --> 00:10:24,380
What's with the sudden change?

156
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:28,520
What a pitiful little sister she is.

157
00:10:28,520 --> 00:10:30,460
Hey, hey, is this guy going
to cry if I keep my distance?

158
00:10:30,460 --> 00:10:30,820
That's right.

159
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:34,300
Don't worry! Matoi doesn't mind at all!

160
00:10:37,060 --> 00:10:37,720
Just as I thought!

161
00:10:39,820 --> 00:10:43,460
Stop crying! A grown man crying is embarrassing!
Everyone in the restaurant is watching!

162
00:10:44,400 --> 00:10:45,800
I'm fine! I'll stop in a moment!

163
00:10:49,020 --> 00:10:52,820
I feel refreshed after crying!
So, what were we talking about?

164
00:10:54,060 --> 00:10:55,060
What's wrong?

165
00:10:55,980 --> 00:10:59,620
Lemon! What's with this guy? His
character is totally different from yours!

166
00:10:59,620 --> 00:11:03,520
Aaaah, he's the type who goes from
gloomy to cheerful and back again.

167
00:11:03,520 --> 00:11:08,720
Everyone in this family is so strange.
I can never get used to them.

168
00:11:21,420 --> 00:11:22,340
Mm.

169
00:11:26,740 --> 00:11:27,660
Mm.

170
00:11:27,660 --> 00:11:28,240
Mm.

171
00:11:28,240 --> 00:11:28,760
Mm.

172
00:11:28,760 --> 00:11:28,880
Mm.

173
00:11:28,880 --> 00:11:29,200
Mm.

174
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:29,600
Mm.

175
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:29,680
Mm.

176
00:11:29,680 --> 00:11:29,980
Mm.

177
00:11:29,980 --> 00:11:30,600
Mm.

178
00:11:37,280 --> 00:11:38,680
Mm.

179
00:11:42,200 --> 00:11:43,600
Mm.

180
00:11:43,600 --> 00:11:44,280
Mm.

181
00:11:44,280 --> 00:11:44,560
Mm.

182
00:11:44,560 --> 00:11:45,820
Mm.

183
00:11:45,820 --> 00:11:46,840
Mm.

184
00:11:46,840 --> 00:11:49,000
Mm.

185
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:49,240
Mm.

186
00:11:49,240 --> 00:11:49,540
Mm.

187
00:11:50,360 --> 00:11:51,060
Mm.

188
00:11:51,060 --> 00:11:51,120
Mm.

189
00:12:08,480 --> 00:12:12,680
Good night.

190
00:12:21,740 --> 00:12:23,700
A mellow, good broth has come out.

191
00:12:23,700 --> 00:12:27,420
It draws out the sweetness and bitterness
of this season's Kyoto vegetables,

192
00:12:27,420 --> 00:12:29,780
and its harmony with the
fish cakes is truly excellent.

193
00:12:33,040 --> 00:12:36,560
As always, having Lemon taste
it makes me a bit nervous.

194
00:12:37,540 --> 00:12:40,500
Yū-san, you've completely
mastered the restaurant's taste.

195
00:12:41,040 --> 00:12:41,620
Really?

196
00:12:42,160 --> 00:12:44,500
Lemon's palate is, you could say,
one in a hundred years,

197
00:12:44,500 --> 00:12:47,300
Gepard said she has an
amazing sense of taste.

198
00:12:47,620 --> 00:12:50,800
She gave her seal of approval,
so be happy, Yū-san.

199
00:12:51,120 --> 00:12:51,460
Yes.

200
00:12:53,180 --> 00:12:56,120
But lately our restaurant has been losing customers,
hasn't it?

201
00:12:56,120 --> 00:12:58,460
Could the customers be tired of this flavor?

202
00:12:58,460 --> 00:13:00,600
You're overthinking it, Yūtsun.

203
00:13:01,040 --> 00:13:03,140
It's because the economy is bad right now.

204
00:13:03,140 --> 00:13:04,520
It's the same at every restaurant.

205
00:13:04,520 --> 00:13:05,540
Yeah, I suppose so.

206
00:13:06,660 --> 00:13:11,760
No, a true chef makes food that brings customers in,
no matter how bad the economy is.

207
00:13:12,380 --> 00:13:14,940
Maybe there's something
wrong with the food I make.

208
00:13:15,880 --> 00:13:17,940
You really do change your mind every five minutes,
don't you?

209
00:13:17,940 --> 00:13:20,560
Have more confidence in your own skills.

210
00:13:21,120 --> 00:13:22,560
Yūtsun is too serious, you know.

211
00:13:23,380 --> 00:13:25,780
Yū-san,
you don't need to brood over it like that.

212
00:13:26,140 --> 00:13:28,840
That's right, your little sister
came all this way to see you.

213
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:32,780
You've got the day off today,
so go somewhere to clear your head.

214
00:13:33,780 --> 00:13:34,800
That sounds good.

215
00:13:35,560 --> 00:13:39,540
That's right, Lemon loves period dramas, so
shall we go to the Kyoto Jidai Geki Village?

216
00:13:39,940 --> 00:13:42,940
Yes, yes!
Lemon absolutely loves period dramas!

217
00:13:47,360 --> 00:13:49,760
I hope we get to see Mito Kōmon,
my favorite!

218
00:13:51,580 --> 00:13:52,560
Sorry to keep you waiting.

219
00:13:52,560 --> 00:13:53,960
Hurry, hurry!

220
00:13:57,560 --> 00:13:58,820
Wow, amazing!

221
00:13:58,820 --> 00:14:02,980
Good thing there's a big
special feature corner.

222
00:14:02,980 --> 00:14:03,820
Let's go.

223
00:14:05,980 --> 00:14:07,640
That brings back memories.

224
00:14:09,140 --> 00:14:12,000
So this is the 32nd year
it's been on the air?

225
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:13,840
Kankichi, you watched it too?

226
00:14:13,840 --> 00:14:15,920
You've been watching it
pretty much from the start.

227
00:14:15,920 --> 00:14:17,980
When did Lemon start watching?

228
00:14:19,100 --> 00:14:20,000
From here on, though.

229
00:14:21,400 --> 00:14:22,200
A year ago?

230
00:14:23,600 --> 00:14:26,640
Come to think of it,
she's still a five-year-old kindergartener.

231
00:14:26,640 --> 00:14:31,640
But she watches the reruns, so she
knows the first and second Kōmon-sama too.

232
00:14:32,220 --> 00:14:32,620
I see.

233
00:14:37,160 --> 00:14:38,360
Are you buying something?

234
00:14:38,580 --> 00:14:40,300
I'm buying a photo of Lord Kōmon.

235
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:42,920
Kankichi.

236
00:14:43,800 --> 00:14:46,920
I wonder which is better,
the Windmill Mansion or Keidō?

237
00:14:46,920 --> 00:14:49,880
Well, I've never really
thought about it much.

238
00:14:51,500 --> 00:14:54,020
I want the Sukesaburo
with the big chest too.

239
00:14:54,020 --> 00:14:55,140
W-who's that?

240
00:14:55,140 --> 00:14:58,000
Don't you know that's Suke-san's real name?

241
00:14:58,000 --> 00:14:59,780
What a pathetic fellow you are.

242
00:14:59,780 --> 00:15:02,720
A fluffy Hachibei

243
00:15:03,440 --> 00:15:05,380
This one's hard to pass up, too.

244
00:15:05,380 --> 00:15:09,220
Either one's fine, isn't it?

245
00:15:09,220 --> 00:15:11,600
At times like this, you just buy them all.

246
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:14,820
Even with a little child's
eyes sparkling like this...

247
00:15:14,820 --> 00:15:16,180
Don't say such insolent things.

248
00:15:16,180 --> 00:15:19,200
Using big words like "insolent" for a brat.

249
00:15:21,180 --> 00:15:22,660
They're selling Gin-Ro too.

250
00:15:24,420 --> 00:15:25,320
*Yawn*

251
00:15:27,540 --> 00:15:29,860
You really do love period dramas, don't you.

252
00:15:31,400 --> 00:15:31,800
Mm?

253
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:40,740
Wow, it's just like on TV!

254
00:15:41,600 --> 00:15:43,080
So this is Edo!

255
00:15:43,560 --> 00:15:46,100
It's the biggest period
drama open set in Japan.

256
00:15:46,100 --> 00:15:47,880
Edo doesn't exist anymore, you know.

257
00:15:47,880 --> 00:15:49,540
Well, it does, right here and now.

258
00:15:51,520 --> 00:15:54,040
Don't the people on TV live here?

259
00:15:54,240 --> 00:15:55,480
No, they don't live here.

260
00:15:56,540 --> 00:15:58,700
But Zenigata Heiji's house is right there.

261
00:16:00,140 --> 00:16:02,700
That was built for location shoots.

262
00:16:02,700 --> 00:16:05,900
How can Lemon read kanji?

263
00:16:06,360 --> 00:16:09,580
I learned from TV.
Grandma has the videos, you see.

264
00:16:10,160 --> 00:16:12,100
See, I know other characters too.

265
00:16:13,180 --> 00:16:15,400
Then try writing "lemon," then.

266
00:16:15,400 --> 00:16:17,417
Um,

267
00:16:17,467 --> 00:16:19,880
I think it went like this...

268
00:16:21,120 --> 00:16:21,680
"Kuni no jidai"

269
00:16:21,680 --> 00:16:24,740
Never mind,
you'll be able to write it someday.

270
00:16:24,740 --> 00:16:26,980
First, learn to write your own name.

271
00:16:26,980 --> 00:16:29,640
One sheet becomes two,
two sheets become four.

272
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:31,380
Yay!

273
00:16:33,360 --> 00:16:34,400
No, come on.

274
00:16:34,400 --> 00:16:35,320
It's fine, it's fine.

275
00:16:38,640 --> 00:16:39,460
Okay, I'm taking it!

276
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:42,240
Okay, stay still just like that.

277
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:45,280
Now, moving on.

278
00:16:45,980 --> 00:16:47,220
Say cheese!

279
00:16:48,540 --> 00:16:49,660
Okay, thanks for your hard work.

280
00:16:50,240 --> 00:16:51,100
The period drama's starting, too.

281
00:16:51,120 --> 00:16:52,980
You can go take a stroll around the village.

282
00:16:52,980 --> 00:16:54,580
I see.

283
00:16:55,160 --> 00:16:57,420
Shall we go, Princess Lemon?

284
00:16:57,940 --> 00:16:59,000
Don't be such a loser.

285
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:00,100
Tōyama Kinshirō

286
00:17:03,280 --> 00:17:04,720
Aww, how cute.

287
00:17:04,720 --> 00:17:06,520
Please take a photo with me.

288
00:17:06,520 --> 00:17:07,140
Please.

289
00:17:09,540 --> 00:17:10,760
Sure, go ahead.

290
00:17:11,680 --> 00:17:12,780
Okay, pose!

291
00:17:13,660 --> 00:17:14,400
Wow.

292
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:16,120
I feel like Mickey Mouse.

293
00:17:21,240 --> 00:17:21,680
What is it?

294
00:17:21,900 --> 00:17:23,760
I'm really fine, honestly.

295
00:17:23,760 --> 00:17:26,400
Honestly, who on earth called an ambulance?

296
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:27,900
You're overreacting.

297
00:17:29,200 --> 00:17:30,500
Hey, what happened?

298
00:17:31,040 --> 00:17:34,980
The actor playing the cook cut his
hand with a knife during the shoot.

299
00:17:34,980 --> 00:17:37,900
Damn it, we can't shoot like this.

300
00:17:37,900 --> 00:17:40,480
Then I've got the perfect guy for it.

301
00:17:40,480 --> 00:17:41,220
Really?

302
00:17:41,960 --> 00:17:42,300
Hey.

303
00:17:44,340 --> 00:17:46,980
I-I can't act, you know!

304
00:17:46,980 --> 00:17:48,920
Cooking is right up your alley, isn't it?

305
00:17:52,880 --> 00:17:55,240
You're pulling it off pretty well,
aren't you?

306
00:17:55,860 --> 00:17:56,780
Is that so?

307
00:17:57,940 --> 00:17:59,300
Thank you for your hard work.

308
00:17:59,920 --> 00:18:03,020
The real Aji no Heikichi!

309
00:18:03,020 --> 00:18:04,940
Aji no Heikichi.

310
00:18:04,940 --> 00:18:09,660
Aren't you Ajihei,
the Aji no Heikichi from Ajitorimono-chō?

311
00:18:11,080 --> 00:18:13,580
I'm sorry to ask,
but please take good care of me.

312
00:18:15,740 --> 00:18:18,720
Yūutsu, Ajihei is begging me this earnestly.

313
00:18:18,720 --> 00:18:21,040
Well then, if we don't help him out,
he'll steal the show!

314
00:18:21,120 --> 00:18:22,420
I-I understand.

315
00:18:22,420 --> 00:18:24,960
Okay, action!

316
00:18:26,680 --> 00:18:27,520
Cut!

317
00:18:28,240 --> 00:18:29,880
You're the best!

318
00:18:30,100 --> 00:18:30,660
Th-thank you.

319
00:18:31,540 --> 00:18:35,240
Next, the scene where Ajihei eats the
duck hotpot in the tatami room, please!

320
00:18:35,960 --> 00:18:37,700
Okay, action!

321
00:18:39,280 --> 00:18:42,160
Lord Ajikawa, it's ready. Please, have some.

322
00:18:42,590 --> 00:18:43,740
Is it?

323
00:18:44,480 --> 00:18:48,240
Chūta, this duck hotpot is exquisite!
Come on, eat!

324
00:18:54,800 --> 00:18:55,920
It is delicious.

325
00:18:56,900 --> 00:18:58,160
So it must be.

326
00:18:59,760 --> 00:19:00,200
Amazing.

327
00:19:00,200 --> 00:19:04,580
Ajihei is truly delighted
eating Yūtsu's cooking.

328
00:19:04,580 --> 00:19:07,540
Kankichi Yūtsu is truly amazing, isn't he.

329
00:19:07,540 --> 00:19:08,200
Cut!

330
00:19:09,380 --> 00:19:10,720
Absolutely perfect.

331
00:19:10,720 --> 00:19:12,000
Thank you for your hard work.

332
00:19:15,280 --> 00:19:18,460
Truly delicious duck hotpot, Gibōshi.

333
00:19:18,460 --> 00:19:19,280
Thank you.

334
00:19:20,480 --> 00:19:21,520
I'm honored.

335
00:19:21,520 --> 00:19:22,840
Can't you be more moved?

336
00:19:24,720 --> 00:19:26,820
Ajihei is a supreme gourmet, you know.

337
00:19:27,380 --> 00:19:29,280
And I was praised by Ajihei.

338
00:19:29,280 --> 00:19:31,520
I'm telling you to rejoice more.

339
00:19:31,520 --> 00:19:32,780
Oh.

340
00:19:34,020 --> 00:19:36,140
Yūtsu is the happiest man in Japan.

341
00:19:36,140 --> 00:19:39,380
Can't you have more confidence
in your own cooking skills?

342
00:19:44,840 --> 00:19:46,280
I'm starting to feel confident, somehow.

343
00:19:46,880 --> 00:19:49,620
Now I want to get back to
the shop and cook even more!

344
00:19:50,280 --> 00:19:52,460
Lemon, sorry,
but I'm leaving the rest to you.

345
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:58,400
Hey, you still have your costume and wig on!

346
00:19:59,300 --> 00:20:01,187
He's already gone.

347
00:20:01,237 --> 00:20:03,880
He's a real roller coaster, that one.

348
00:20:05,540 --> 00:20:08,613
Heh, I got Ajihei's autograph!

349
00:20:08,663 --> 00:20:10,800
I'll treasure it for the
rest of my life, though.

350
00:20:11,040 --> 00:20:13,520
You really do love period dramas, don't you.

351
00:20:13,960 --> 00:20:16,700
They're filming another scene.

352
00:20:16,750 --> 00:20:18,320
Let's go, Kankichi.

353
00:20:19,080 --> 00:20:19,480
Right.

354
00:20:20,560 --> 00:20:22,240
What's the matter, Kankichi?

355
00:20:25,220 --> 00:20:26,300
Those guys

356
00:20:26,300 --> 00:20:27,900
Hey!

357
00:20:27,900 --> 00:20:31,400
Nice.

358
00:20:31,400 --> 00:20:33,460
I almost left Lemon alone again.

359
00:20:35,320 --> 00:20:36,500
Just borrowing this.

360
00:20:37,420 --> 00:20:40,100
Cue the music!

361
00:20:41,220 --> 00:20:42,640
Hello, everyone!

362
00:20:43,440 --> 00:20:45,380
I'm in Kyoto right now.

363
00:20:46,700 --> 00:20:48,780
Here at the Uzumasa Jidai Geki Village,

364
00:20:48,780 --> 00:20:51,180
the latest in the Mito Kōmon series

365
00:20:52,240 --> 00:20:55,220
filming is progressing smoothly.

366
00:20:55,860 --> 00:20:57,660
Mito Kōmon, Chief?

367
00:20:57,660 --> 00:21:00,860
We're doing an on-site report on it.

368
00:21:02,060 --> 00:21:04,060
Senpai, you're in Kyoto too, right?

369
00:21:04,060 --> 00:21:07,080
If it's Ryotsu,
he's definitely out playing around.

370
00:21:07,640 --> 00:21:08,600
So basically, here...

371
00:21:12,580 --> 00:21:14,940
Kōmon-sama is in danger!

372
00:21:14,940 --> 00:21:16,740
Got it. Hold on tight!

373
00:21:23,400 --> 00:21:23,940
Whoa!

374
00:21:24,200 --> 00:21:25,140
We're done for!

375
00:21:25,380 --> 00:21:26,200
Even Lemon-chan!

376
00:21:26,300 --> 00:21:28,160
Why is Ryotsu on TV...

377
00:21:28,160 --> 00:21:29,760
Really!

378
00:21:30,760 --> 00:21:46,320
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu...

379
00:21:46,320 --> 00:22:02,660
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee!

380
00:22:02,660 --> 00:22:05,240
Get off the screen before
they cut to a close-up!

381
00:22:07,020 --> 00:22:08,060
Who are these people?

382
00:22:08,680 --> 00:22:10,760
They're a wanted theft ring.

383
00:22:10,760 --> 00:22:13,080
And you?

384
00:22:14,500 --> 00:22:15,700
I'm just a guy like that.

385
00:22:17,380 --> 00:22:20,220
He's totally getting carried away.

386
00:22:20,220 --> 00:22:22,980
We had an unexpected
big arrest during filming.

387
00:22:22,980 --> 00:22:24,720
It was quite the incident.

388
00:22:24,720 --> 00:22:26,560
Are you with the Kyoto Prefectural Police?

389
00:22:27,200 --> 00:22:29,180
No, it's Edo Sakura, obviously.

390
00:22:29,180 --> 00:22:30,400
Even crying children go quiet.

391
00:22:31,480 --> 00:22:34,740
It's the three golds of Katsushika
Precinct and Kankichi Ryotsu.

392
00:22:35,780 --> 00:22:37,000
They've stripped off.

393
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:37,920
Tattoos first.

394
00:22:37,920 --> 00:22:40,720
Isn't that Chief Ohara
and the station chief?

395
00:22:40,720 --> 00:22:42,160
Those tattoos...

396
00:22:42,160 --> 00:22:43,860
They had them drawn on just now.

397
00:22:44,380 --> 00:22:46,500
Our station chief and the Chief.

398
00:22:46,500 --> 00:22:48,620
They've got doodled-on faces, don't they?

399
00:22:51,640 --> 00:22:54,080
This Chief Ohara is...

400
00:22:54,080 --> 00:22:57,920
a hopeless boss who does
nothing but nag and yell.

401
00:23:02,900 --> 00:23:04,300
I can't take it anymore, can I?

402
00:23:04,300 --> 00:23:05,440
Hurry and make them stop.

403
00:23:07,060 --> 00:23:09,420
That last part was bad, so cut it.

404
00:23:10,640 --> 00:23:13,380
By the way,
when is this report going to air?

405
00:23:13,380 --> 00:23:14,420
It's live, though.

406
00:23:14,420 --> 00:23:17,460
So if it's live...

407
00:23:20,820 --> 00:23:21,300
Yes.

408
00:23:21,300 --> 00:23:24,360
Steppy Chief's head is steaming.

409
00:23:26,620 --> 00:23:28,260
He just stood up.

410
00:23:28,920 --> 00:23:31,320
Kyu-tsu, just you wait!

411
00:23:32,020 --> 00:23:34,340
He suddenly ran off super fast.

412
00:23:35,580 --> 00:23:37,420
It was all a joke, okay?

413
00:23:37,420 --> 00:23:39,200
Well, I'm busy, so I'll be going now.

414
00:23:39,200 --> 00:23:41,340
Let's go, Lemon.

415
00:23:41,340 --> 00:23:42,420
Wait a second.

416
00:23:44,060 --> 00:23:47,360
Kankichi, Lord Kōmon thanked us!

417
00:23:47,360 --> 00:23:48,900
Lemon is so happy.

418
00:23:48,900 --> 00:23:51,160
That's great, let's hurry and go home.

419
00:23:51,160 --> 00:23:53,300
Before the Chief shows up.

420
00:23:54,360 --> 00:23:55,220
Let me hear the radio!

421
00:23:57,580 --> 00:24:02,060
I will never forgive you this time,
no matter what!

422
00:24:24,360 --> 00:24:27,340
Maybe I just don't want to become one

423
00:24:27,340 --> 00:24:31,980
If I'm dawdling at the street corner

424
00:24:31,980 --> 00:24:34,320
the moon has slipped away

425
00:24:34,320 --> 00:24:38,180
because now isn't everything

426
00:24:38,180 --> 00:24:42,000
don't get too worked up

427
00:24:42,740 --> 00:24:46,280
even if I lie and cheat a little

428
00:24:46,880 --> 00:24:50,440
once in a while, helping someone

429
00:24:50,440 --> 00:24:52,480
Baby do you know me?

430
00:24:54,360 --> 00:24:56,660
A nice spirit

431
00:24:57,900 --> 00:25:01,820
I won't rot, I'll do what I have to do

432
00:25:01,820 --> 00:25:04,300
A cute spirit

433
00:25:05,000 --> 00:25:07,720
What's hard to understand is

434
00:25:08,680 --> 00:25:11,460
That's just how I want to look.

435
00:25:12,500 --> 00:25:17,220
Better than all show, don't you think?

436
00:25:30,440 --> 00:25:33,800
Honda and Otohime,
the best couple everyone envies,

437
00:25:33,800 --> 00:25:36,400
but their hearts are drifting apart.

438
00:25:36,400 --> 00:25:37,800
Alright, leave it to me!

439
00:25:37,800 --> 00:25:40,040
At times like this, order some food!

440
00:25:40,040 --> 00:25:43,320
I'm a master of romance,
so there's no doubt about it.

441
00:25:43,320 --> 00:25:45,780
The first step of love.

442
00:25:45,780 --> 00:25:46,980
Hope we get along.

443
00:25:55,200 --> 00:25:59,180
Everyone, come to our town!

444
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:00,740
Thank you.

